ord":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"The evidence mapping records a Lean proof of exactly this statement. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-purely-periodic-support"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-purely-periodic-support"],"id":"long.thm-purely-periodic-support","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 5.5 (Purely periodic support)","locator":"Long record Theorem 5.5, p. 39, label thm:purely-periodic-support","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For integers $b\\ge2$ and $m\\ge1$, and every $m$-periodic $A\\subseteq\\mathbb N$ (i.e. $n+m \\in A \\Leftrightarrow n \\in A$ for all $n$) containing a positive element, the support series $\\sum_{a\\in A,\\ a\\ge1}(b^a-1)^{-1}$ is irrational. **Hypotheses:** $b \\ge 2$, $m \\ge 1$, $A$ $m$-periodic, $\\exists a > 0,\\ a \\in A$.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-purely-periodic-support","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-purely-periodic-support","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.thm-purely-periodic-support%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.irrational_erdosSupportSeries_periodic%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.thm-purely-periodic-support%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.irrational_erdosSupportSeries_periodic%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.irrational_erdosSupportSeries_periodic"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-purely-periodic-support","id":"field:12c717f31d44